#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc04f720-28f3-55ab-8e89-582db57672a4" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Limit at Infinity of a General Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7e93ad7-3079-55cc-a243-3df0165226b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7e93ad7-3079-55cc-a243-3df0165226b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264561} :answer-field/id #uuid "958887a5-800c-57f0-977f-c87b76df8b8c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264560}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5b8c1c1a-9fbe-5ca4-ab19-913625610f78" :question/math-academy-id "q-166216" :question/problem "Consider the quadratic function $f(x)=4-{x}^{2}.$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We identify the leading term of the polynomial and compute its limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }(4-{x}^{2}) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }(-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }({x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-(\\infty ) \\\\  & =-\\infty \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264562 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a441c8ef-b5b3-5438-97b9-53e4eb7b2d75" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Numerator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58d9e57e-f446-5415-8893-879950cf8d7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58d9e57e-f446-5415-8893-879950cf8d7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264564} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ad08d2e-4cb8-52a6-b31d-060fd0512bde" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264563}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "386145e1-97c4-5291-9ae5-69c49e55606b" :question/math-academy-id "q-166217" :question/problem "Consider the quadratic function $f(x)=4-{x}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nEvaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}.$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit directly by substituting $x=2,$ we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{4-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{2}}{4-{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since there is a radical in the numerator, we can evaluate the limit by first multiplying the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{4-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{(\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x})(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})}{(4-{x}^{2})(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{2-x}{(2+x)(2-x)(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\cancel{2-x}}{(2+x)\\cancel{(2-x)}(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{1}{(2+x)(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(2+2)(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4(2\\sqrt{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264565 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8f2e684-6cd8-5ede-9f70-1a24ada54cb9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Instantaneous Rate of Change of a Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3c1dd50-e591-5613-af40-d7e93107918e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3c1dd50-e591-5613-af40-d7e93107918e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264567} :answer-field/id #uuid "6feff4d0-fd8f-5dbe-88e1-8b146ccab997" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264566}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3780e331-ad54-57c9-a1d3-183beea2fe73" :question/math-academy-id "q-166218" :question/problem "Consider the quadratic function $f(x)=4-{x}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nEvaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}.$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{16}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change of $f(x)$ at $x=2$ is given by\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(2)={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{f(x)-f(2)}{x-2}=-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x\\,+$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Simplifying the expression under the limit, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(2) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{f(x)-f(2)}{x-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{[4-{x}^{2}]-[4-{2}^{2}]}{x-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{4-{x}^{2}}{x-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{-({x}^{2}-4)}{x-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{-(x+2)(x-2)}{x-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{-(x+2)\\cancel{(x-2)}}{\\cancel{x-2}} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264568 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dad9bdc2-a243-5437-8904-9906c2d9a90e" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Sum Rule to Compute a Limit"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19f3e57f-e7d9-5066-82ea-71f1ea048eba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19f3e57f-e7d9-5066-82ea-71f1ea048eba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264570} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a67106d-cec3-5377-959c-c4a71f377ac4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264569}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ebe30ec3-c953-590f-bd21-c20f02ee1f83" :question/math-academy-id "q-166219" :question/problem "Consider the quadratic function $f(x)=4-{x}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nEvaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}.$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{16}$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change of $f(x)$ at $x=2$ is given by\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(2)={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{f(x)-f(2)}{x-2}=-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x\\,+$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$).$\n\nCurrent part:\n\n$-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\,(x+2)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first apply the sum rule, and then apply the constant rule and compute the limits of the power functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\,(x+2) & =-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}x-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}2 \\\\  & =-2-2 \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c6f3c71-d11b-59af-bad6-5f5c0ff6634f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94dd5fb0-d678-5d32-896d-1021b98814e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94dd5fb0-d678-5d32-896d-1021b98814e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264573} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a46f348-6137-5ac0-b013-1d7682ea2b82" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264572}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a63e24a-e04b-5db9-bbc1-e9ee3edfd2ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-166220" :question/problem "Consider the quadratic function $f(x)=4-{x}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nEvaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}.$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{16}$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change of $f(x)$ at $x=2$ is given by\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(2)={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{f(x)-f(2)}{x-2}=-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x\\,+$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$).$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\n$-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\,(x+2)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-4$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe derivative of $f(x)$ is defined by\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$-\\,h\\,).$" :question/worked-solution "Simplifying the expression under the limit, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{4-(x+h)^{2}-[4-{x}^{2}]}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{4-{x}^{2}-2xh-{h}^{2}-4+{x}^{2}}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{-2xh-{h}^{2}}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{h(-2x-h)}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{\\cancel{h}(-2x-h)}{\\cancel{h}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}(-2x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264574 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dad9bdc2-a243-5437-8904-9906c2d9a90e" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Sum Rule to Compute a Limit"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d3556e3-e7df-5190-a5a9-501d11c6af92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264576}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d3556e3-e7df-5190-a5a9-501d11c6af92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264576} :answer-field/id #uuid "3901e99e-4aa4-56ec-b3f4-2f7a4539d9a8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264575}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ac45f5dc-89a8-58c4-87b2-3434a292dff7" :question/math-academy-id "q-166221" :question/problem "Consider the quadratic function $f(x)=4-{x}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nEvaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}.$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{16}$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change of $f(x)$ at $x=2$ is given by\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(2)={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{f(x)-f(2)}{x-2}=-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x\\,+$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$).$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\n$-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\,(x+2)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-4$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nThe derivative of $f(x)$ is defined by\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-2x$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$-\\,h\\,).$\n\nCurrent part:\n\n${f}^{′}(x)={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}(-2x-h)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first apply the sum rule, and then apply the constant rule and compute the limits of the power functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{h\\to \\,0}(-2x-h) & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}(-2x)-{lim}_{h\\to \\,0}h \\\\  & =-2x{lim}_{h\\to \\,0}1-{lim}_{h\\to \\,0}h \\\\  & =-2x-0 \\\\  & =-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264577 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f0efa50-9154-5cf3-bf01-e1b6eead489d" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Right Riemann Sum With Regular Step Size"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8cff3fd-3773-555e-9f9f-e31462ceb14b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8cff3fd-3773-555e-9f9f-e31462ceb14b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264579} :answer-field/id #uuid "3db12b72-7f80-5853-af4b-34f8489452e5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264578}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0372052e-053c-559a-b9eb-2075e647da29" :question/math-academy-id "q-166222" :question/problem "Consider the quadratic function $f(x)=4-{x}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nEvaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}.$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{16}$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change of $f(x)$ at $x=2$ is given by\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(2)={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{f(x)-f(2)}{x-2}=-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x\\,+$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$).$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\n$-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\,(x+2)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-4$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nThe derivative of $f(x)$ is defined by\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-2x$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$-\\,h\\,).$\n\nEarlier part 6:\n\n${f}^{′}(x)={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}(-2x-h)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-2x$\n\nCurrent part:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950896/assets/19d0c50eff5613451c833c00e2d151b93ca5d7e490366fc811d6730e383227de.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above (not drawn to scale). Estimate the area $A$ using a right Riemann sum with step size $Δx=0.5.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A\\,≈\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch our situation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950896/assets/e13444351bb092ced6fc788ae921622f154a267e9544e928700736a53a259fc6.png)\n\nThe area $A$ under the graph can be approximated using the right Riemann sum with step size $Δx=0.5,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nA≈(\\overset{\\text{heights}}{\\overset{⏞}{f(0.5)+f(1)+f(1.5)+f(2)}})\\cdot {{Δx}_{⏟}}_{\\text{width}}\n$$\n\nSo, we now set up a table with the values of $f(x)$ at each point:\n\n| $x$ | $0.5$ | $1$ | $1.5$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $3.75$ | $3$ | $1.75$ | $0$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain the following approximation for our area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈(3.75+3+1.75+0)\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =8.5\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =4.25\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264580 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d01d6ed-1c25-5170-a1ad-7a4fa0103db7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Right Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "746029fa-3599-590c-9f99-c62801f49b2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264582}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "746029fa-3599-590c-9f99-c62801f49b2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264582} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e32efa9-400e-593e-9b27-f5ce542becbe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264581}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3d9d3fe9-2259-5414-99ae-3627c722db65" :question/math-academy-id "q-166223" :question/problem "Consider the quadratic function $f(x)=4-{x}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nEvaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}.$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{16}$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change of $f(x)$ at $x=2$ is given by\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(2)={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{f(x)-f(2)}{x-2}=-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x\\,+$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$).$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\n$-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\,(x+2)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-4$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nThe derivative of $f(x)$ is defined by\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-2x$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$-\\,h\\,).$\n\nEarlier part 6:\n\n${f}^{′}(x)={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}(-2x-h)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-2x$\n\nEarlier part 7:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950896/assets/19d0c50eff5613451c833c00e2d151b93ca5d7e490366fc811d6730e383227de.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above (not drawn to scale). Estimate the area $A$ using a right Riemann sum with step size $Δx=0.5.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A\\,≈\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4.25$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nWrite the expression for the Riemann sum from part 7 in sigma notation.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The right Riemann sum $\\,=\\,0.5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}(4-$  \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         ${i}^{2})$" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nIn our case, we have $n=4$ subintervals, $a=0,$ $b=2,$ and $Δx=0.5.$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(0+i\\cdot 0.5)\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(0.5i) \\\\  & =0.5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}(4-{(0.5i)}^{2}) \\\\  & =0.5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}(4-0.25{i}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264583 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89902023-09e6-50cd-b08a-9d3e82d826c9" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Area Bounded by a Curve as a Definite Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1169cd4-fbef-58a1-80ad-0edfa1889e30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-x^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1169cd4-fbef-58a1-80ad-0edfa1889e30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-x^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264585} :answer-field/id #uuid "10c24635-fa09-554e-870b-16082908843f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264584} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2fb2e94-7aa0-50c4-8ea4-deb961cfbca8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2fb2e94-7aa0-50c4-8ea4-deb961cfbca8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264587} :answer-field/id #uuid "633d083b-e4e2-530a-9f8f-57911663bda8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264586} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf61c88e-0608-563c-adf7-72553e2bd57d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :